{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\n#define len(c) static_cast<int>((c).size())\n\ni64 compute_gcd(i64 u, i64 v) {\n    while (v != 0) {\n        u %= v;\n        swap(u, v);\n    }\n    return u;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    i64 numerator, denominator, limit;\n    cin >> numerator >> denominator >> limit;\n\n    i64 best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n    double min_diff = 1e18;\n\n    for (i64 d = 1; d <= limit; ++d) {\n        i64 num1 = 0;\n        i64 lo = 0, hi = 100000;\n        while (lo <= hi) {\n            i64 mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            if (mid * denominator <= numerator * d) {\n                num1 = mid;\n                lo = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                hi = mid - 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        i64 num2 = 0;\n        lo = 0, hi = 100000;\n        while (lo <= hi) {\n            i64 mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            if (mid * denominator < numerator * d) {\n                lo = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                num2 = mid;\n                hi = mid - 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        double diff1 = fabs(static_cast<double>(num1) / d - static_cast<double>(numerator) / denominator);\n        double diff2 = fabs(static_cast<double>(num2) / d - static_cast<double>(numerator) / denominator);\n\n        i64 candidate_num = num1;\n        i64 candidate_den = d;\n        double current_diff = diff1;\n\n        if (diff2 + 1e-9 < current_diff) {\n            candidate_num = num2;\n            candidate_den = d;\n            current_diff = diff2;\n        }\n\n        i64 g = compute_gcd(candidate_num, candidate_den);\n        candidate_num /= g;\n        candidate_den /= g;\n\n        if (current_diff < min_diff) {\n            best_num = candidate_num;\n            best_den = candidate_den;\n            min_diff = current_diff;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\n\ndef compute_gcd(u, v):\n    while v != 0:\n        u %= v\n        u, v = v, u\n    return u\n\ndef main():\n    numerator, denominator, limit = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    best_num = 0\n    best_den = 1\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    \n    for d in range(1, limit + 1):\n        # Binary search for num1: largest num such that num * denominator <= numerator * d\n        lo, hi = 0, 100000\n        num1 = 0\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if mid * denominator <= numerator * d:\n                num1 = mid\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        \n        # Binary search for num2: smallest num such that num * denominator >= numerator * d\n        lo, hi = 0, 100000\n        num2 = 0\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if mid * denominator < numerator * d:\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                num2 = mid\n                hi = mid - 1\n        \n        diff1 = abs(num1 / d - numerator / denominator)\n        diff2 = abs(num2 / d - numerator / denominator)\n        \n        candidate_num = num1\n        candidate_den = d\n        current_diff = diff1\n        \n        if diff2 + 1e-9 < current_diff:\n            candidate_num = num2\n            candidate_den = d\n            current_diff = diff2\n        \n        g = compute_gcd(candidate_num, candidate_den)\n        candidate_num //= g\n        candidate_den //= g\n        \n        if current_diff < min_diff:\n            best_num = candidate_num\n            best_den = candidate_den\n            min_diff = current_diff\n    \n    print(f\"{best_num}/{best_den}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.929640509653836e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.002504785545170307, -0.02984842285513878, -0.5233494639396667, -1.0490362910786644e-05, -0.0022156708873808384, -8.583032467868179e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -4.172316494077677e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576272320060525e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -0.003789032343775034, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -6.12716976320371e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -5.364403477869928e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00027855331427417696, -1.4781842764932662e-05, -2.539125671319198e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.06826169043779373, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.38418